---
import plants from "../data/plants.json";
import partners from "../data/affiliatePartners.json";
import plantArtEntries from "../data/plantArt.json";
import "../styles/global.css";

const plantCount = Array.isArray(plants) ? plants.length : 0;
const blogArticles = [
  {
    slug: "right-plant-right-place",
    title: "Right Plant, Right Place: How to Match Plants to the Space You Actually Have",
    excerpt:
      "Learn how to read light, soil, space, and climate before choosing plants that can actually thrive where you put them.",
    category: "Garden planning",
    tags: ["right plant right place", "garden planning", "light", "soil", "plant selection"],
    body: [
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "After more than thirty years with my hands in the dirt, I can tell you the single most expensive mistake gardeners make has nothing to do with money. It's putting the wrong plant in the wrong spot. That gorgeous hydrangea you bought on impulse will sulk and scorch in your west-facing front bed. The tomato you tucked into a shady corner will give you exactly two sad fruits all summer. The Japanese maple your neighbor swears by will struggle if your soil drains like a clay bowl."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "The old British gardening adage gets it exactly right: <em>right plant, right place</em>. Get that match wrong, and no amount of fertilizer, pampering, or hopeful watering will save you. Get it right, and the plant largely takes care of itself."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Here's how to read your space honestly and choose plants that will actually thrive in it."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Start by reading the light, not the catalog" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Before you look at a single plant tag, spend a weekend watching how light moves across the space you want to plant. Most failures I see come from people guessing at their light."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "The standard categories are deceptively simple. <strong>Full sun</strong> means six or more hours of direct sun, ideally including the strong midday hours. <strong>Part sun</strong> runs roughly four to six hours, with a preference for morning light. <strong>Part shade</strong> is the same hour count but with the harsher afternoon light filtered or blocked. <strong>Full shade</strong> is less than four hours of direct sun, often dappled light all day."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          'The trap is that "full sun" in coastal Maine is not the same as "full sun" in the Mississippi Delta. A plant rated for full sun in a Vermont catalog may fry on an exposed south-facing wall in Memphis. In hot southern climates, give "full sun" plants some afternoon relief and they\'ll reward you. Conversely, "shade-tolerant" perennials in the upper Midwest often need more light than their tag suggests if you\'re growing them in the Pacific Northwest\'s overcast spring.'
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Stand in your space at 9 a.m., noon, and 4 p.m. on a sunny day. Take photos. That's your real light reading."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Know your zone, but don't worship it" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "The USDA Hardiness Zone map tells you the average annual minimum winter temperature in your area. That matters for perennials, shrubs, and trees because it tells you whether a plant will survive your worst cold snap."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "But hardiness zones don't tell you about summer heat, humidity, length of growing season, or the dreaded freeze-thaw cycles of late winter that kill more plants in the transitional South than any deep freeze. A plant rated hardy to Zone 5 may technically survive your Zone 7 winter and still die in August because it can't handle 95-degree nights."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "If you garden in the South or anywhere with brutal summers, pay attention to the AHS Heat Zone map alongside your hardiness zone. And talk to people gardening within twenty miles of you. Local knowledge beats any map."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Understand your soil before you fight it" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Dig a hole. Squeeze a handful of damp soil. If it ribbons out smooth and sticky, you have clay. If it falls apart immediately and feels gritty, you have sand. Most of us have something in between, called loam, with varying amounts of organic matter."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "The bigger question is drainage. Dig a hole roughly a foot deep and a foot wide, fill it with water, let it drain, fill it again, and time how long the second filling takes to drain. If it's gone in two to three hours, you have good drainage. If water is still sitting there after twelve hours, you have a drainage problem that will rot the roots of most ornamentals and nearly every Mediterranean herb."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "You can amend soil at the margins, but you cannot fundamentally change the soil on a half-acre lot. So instead of fighting it, match plants to what you have. Clay soils suit oaks, viburnums, hydrangeas, daylilies, and most of the rose family. Sandy soils favor lavender, rosemary, yarrow, rudbeckia, and many natives adapted to drier conditions. Wet spots are perfect for river birch, swamp milkweed, Joe Pye weed, and bald cypress."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "A cheap soil test from your county extension office will tell you pH and major nutrients for around fifteen dollars. Do it before you spend money on plants. Blueberries need acidic soil. Lilacs prefer alkaline. Knowing your pH saves heartbreak."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Match the plant's mature size to your space honestly" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          'This is where people lie to themselves more than anywhere else. That cute little Leyland cypress in the one-gallon pot wants to be sixty feet tall and twenty feet wide. The "dwarf" Alberta spruce will eventually outgrow most foundation beds. The crepe myrtle the previous owner planted three feet from the house was a mistake before you even bought the place.'
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Read the mature size on the tag and believe it. Then look at where you're planting and ask whether you actually have that much room without crowding, without blocking windows, without growing into power lines, and without forcing you to butcher the plant every spring to keep it in bounds."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "A useful rule for foundation plantings: take the mature width and place the plant at least half that distance from the wall. A shrub that will be six feet wide needs to be planted three feet out from the foundation, minimum."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Think about what the space asks of the plant" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Different spaces have different jobs. Be honest about what you actually want."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "A front foundation bed needs year-round structure, since it's the first thing visitors see in February. Think evergreens, plants with good winter form, and a layered design that doesn't go to mush in cold months. A back patio bed can lean heavily on summer performers because that's when you're actually sitting there. A driveway strip facing reflected heat and road salt is one of the toughest spots in any landscape and demands tough plants - yarrow, sedum, ornamental grasses, juniper. A spot under a mature oak is dry, root-competitive shade, which is hostile to most plants but loved by hostas, hellebores, epimedium, and native woodland ephemerals."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Match the plant's strengths to the season and conditions you most need it to perform."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Build in layers, not in single specimens" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "The most common amateur design mistake is buying one of this and one of that. The result looks like a plant collection rather than a garden."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Professionals design in layers and in odd-numbered drifts. A bed reads well when it has a backdrop layer (often shrubs or tall grasses), a midlayer of substantial perennials, and a front layer of lower-growing edging plants. Repeat the same plant in groups of three, five, or seven rather than dotting singletons around. The eye reads repetition as intentional. It reads variety without repetition as chaos."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Choose natives where you can, and don't be a purist about it" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "Native plants - meaning species that evolved in your region - generally need less water, less fertilizer, and less fussing once established. They also support local insects and birds in ways that hybrids and imports often cannot. The research on this is clear and getting clearer."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "That said, you don't have to plant only natives to garden responsibly. A landscape that's seventy percent native and thirty percent well-chosen non-natives still does enormous ecological good and gives you the design flexibility most people want. The plants to avoid are the invasive non-natives that escape gardens and damage natural areas - Bradford pear, Japanese honeysuckle, English ivy, nandina in the South, Norway maple in the North. Your state's invasive species list will tell you what to skip."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "Plan for the first three years, then for the next thirty" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "A common saying among horticulturists: the first year a perennial sleeps, the second year it creeps, the third year it leaps. Most woody plants follow a similar pattern. The garden you plant this spring will not look like much this fall. It may not look like much next fall either. Plan accordingly, water deeply through the first two summers, and resist the urge to rip things out before they've had a chance to establish."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "At the same time, think about what your design will be in twenty years. Trees will be huge. Some shrubs will need rejuvenation pruning or replacement. Perennials will need dividing. A good garden is a slow conversation between you and the place, not a one-time installation."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "A simple framework when you're standing at the nursery" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "When you're tempted to buy a plant you fell in love with on sight, run through this checklist before you walk to the register:"
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "How many hours of direct sun does the spot get, honestly. What is the mature size of this plant, and do I have that much room. What does my soil look like, and does this plant want what I have. Will this plant survive my coldest winter and my hottest summer. Is it on my state's invasive list. Do I have three or five of these to plant together, or am I about to buy a lonely singleton."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "If you can answer all six confidently, buy the plant. If you can't, take a photo, go home, and do the homework."
      },
      { kind: "heading", text: "The long view" },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "The best gardens I've ever seen weren't designed by people with the most money or the rarest plants. They were designed by people who watched their land carefully for a year before they planted anything serious, who learned what their place actually was, and who chose plants that wanted to be there."
      },
      {
        kind: "p",
        html:
          "That patience is the closest thing to a secret there is in gardening. Right plant, right place. Everything else is detail."
      }
    ]
  }
];
const stripHtml = (value) => String(value).replace(/<[^>]*>/g, " ");
const blogSearchData = blogArticles.map((article) => ({
  slug: article.slug,
  searchableText: [
    article.title,
    article.excerpt,
    article.category,
    article.tags.join(" "),
    ...article.body.map((block) => block.html ?? block.text ?? "")
  ]
    .map(stripHtml)
    .join(" ")
    .toLowerCase()
}));
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Enter a ZIP code and growing conditions to get ranked plant recommendations with nursery links."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,600;9..144,750&family=Inter:wght@400;500;650;750;850&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>What Should I Grow | ZIP-Based Plant Matcher</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="app-shell">
      <nav class="site-tabs" aria-label="Primary sections" role="tablist">
        <button
          class="site-tab is-active"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          aria-selected="true"
          aria-controls="matcher-view"
          data-view="matcher"
        >
          Plant matcher
        </button>
        <button
          class="site-tab"
          type="button"
          role="tab"
          aria-selected="false"
          aria-controls="blog-view"
          data-view="blog"
        >
          Blog
        </button>
      </nav>

      <div id="matcher-view" class="view-panel is-active" role="tabpanel" data-view-panel="matcher">
      <section class="workspace" aria-labelledby="app-title">
        <div class="intro-panel">
          <div class="brand-lockup" aria-label="What Should I Grow">
            <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>What Should I Grow</span>
          </div>
          <h1 id="app-title">What should I grow here?</h1>
          <p>
            Enter your ZIP code and a few garden conditions. Get a ranked field-guide of edible,
            wildlife-friendly, useful, and good-looking plants that are actually worth considering.
          </p>
          <figure class="hero-plate hero-gallery" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="hero-frame" style="--hero-image: url('/plant-art/fig.webp'); --i: 0"></span>
            <span class="hero-frame" style="--hero-image: url('/plant-art/blueberry.webp'); --i: 1"></span>
            <span class="hero-frame" style="--hero-image: url('/plant-art/persimmon.webp'); --i: 2"></span>
            <span class="hero-frame" style="--hero-image: url('/plant-art/plum.webp'); --i: 3"></span>
            <span class="hero-frame" style="--hero-image: url('/plant-art/elderberry.webp'); --i: 4"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-a is-first" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/serviceberry.webp'); --i: 0"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-b is-first" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/raspberry.webp'); --i: 0"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-c is-first" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/generic-vine.webp'); --i: 0"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-a" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/grape.webp'); --i: 1"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-b" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/hardy-kiwi.webp'); --i: 1"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-c" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/gooseberry.webp'); --i: 1"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-a" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/plum.webp'); --i: 2"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-b" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/maypop-passionfruit.webp'); --i: 2"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-c" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/aronia.webp'); --i: 2"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-a" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/blackberry.webp'); --i: 3"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-b" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/blueberry.webp'); --i: 3"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-c" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/elderberry.webp'); --i: 3"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-a" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/fig.webp'); --i: 4"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-b" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/persimmon.webp'); --i: 4"></span>
            <span class="hero-specimen hero-specimen-c" style="--specimen-image: url('/plant-art/generic-flower-herb.webp'); --i: 4"></span>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <form class="matcher-panel" id="matcher-form">
          <div class="form-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">Plot conditions</p>
            <h2>Start with your place.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="zip-row">
            <div>
              <label for="zip">ZIP code</label>
              <p>Hardiness zone anchors the ranking.</p>
            </div>
            <input
              id="zip"
              name="zip"
              inputmode="numeric"
              pattern="[0-9]{5}"
              maxlength="5"
              autocomplete="postal-code"
              placeholder="75001"
              required
            />
            <div id="zone-preview" class="zone-preview" hidden></div>
          </div>

          <fieldset>
            <legend>Sun exposure</legend>
            <div class="segmented">
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="sun" value="full" checked />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Full</span><span class="option-help">6+ hours</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="sun" value="partial" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Partial</span><span class="option-help">3-6 hours</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="sun" value="shade" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Shade</span><span class="option-help">Mostly indirect</span></span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset>
            <legend>Soil type</legend>
            <div class="segmented">
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="soil" value="clay" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Clay</span><span class="option-help">Sticky, holds water</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="soil" value="loam" checked />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Loam</span><span class="option-help">Crumbly, balanced</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="soil" value="sandy" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Sandy</span><span class="option-help">Gritty, drains fast</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="soil" value="not-sure" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Not sure</span><span class="option-help">Uses loam</span></span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset>
            <legend>Water availability</legend>
            <div class="segmented">
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="water" value="low" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Low</span><span class="option-help">Dry spells</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="water" value="medium" checked />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Medium</span><span class="option-help">Normal watering</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="water" value="high" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">High</span><span class="option-help">Moist beds</span></span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset>
            <legend>Goal</legend>
            <div class="segmented goal-grid">
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="goal" value="fruit" checked />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Fruit</span><span class="option-help">Trees, vines, and berries</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="goal" value="vegetables-herbs" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Vegetables &amp; herbs</span><span class="option-help">What you'd plant for the kitchen</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="goal" value="pollinators-wildlife" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Pollinators &amp; wildlife</span><span class="option-help">Feed bees, birds, and butterflies</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="goal" value="curb-appeal" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Curb appeal &amp; color</span><span class="option-help">Plants that earn their spot out front</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="goal" value="privacy-screening" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Privacy &amp; screening</span><span class="option-help">Hide a fence, block a view, soften a line</span></span>
              </label>
              <label>
                <input type="radio" name="goal" value="low-maintenance-natives" />
                <span class="option-card"><span class="option-label">Low-maintenance natives</span><span class="option-help">Tough plants that belong here</span></span>
              </label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <button class="match-button" type="submit">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M11 20a9 9 0 1 1 7.03-3.38l3.17 3.17-1.41 1.41-3.17-3.17A8.96 8.96 0 0 1 11 20Zm0-2a7 7 0 1 0 0-14 7 7 0 0 0 0 14Z"></path>
            </svg>
            Find plants
          </button>
        </form>
      </section>

      <section class="results-band" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="results-head">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Ranked picks</p>
            <h2 id="results-title">Enter a ZIP code to start.</h2>
          </div>
          <p id="zone-note">Not sure about soil defaults to loam. Recommendations are practical starting points, not local extension advice.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="status" class="status"></div>
        <ol id="results" class="results-grid"></ol>
        <div class="results-actions">
          <button id="save-list" class="save-list-button" type="button" hidden>Save this list</button>
          <button id="see-more" class="see-more-button" type="button" hidden>See more results</button>
        </div>
      </section>
      </div>

      <section
        id="blog-view"
        class="view-panel blog-view"
        role="tabpanel"
        data-view-panel="blog"
        aria-labelledby="blog-title"
        hidden
      >
        <div class="blog-shell">
          <header class="blog-hero">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Field notes</p>
              <h1 id="blog-title">Blog</h1>
              <p>
                Practical growing notes for matching plants to real yards, real weather,
                and the space you actually have.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="blog-search">
              <label for="article-search">Search articles</label>
              <input id="article-search" type="search" placeholder="Search by topic, tag, or text" />
            </div>
          </header>

          <div id="article-list" class="article-list">
            {blogArticles.map((article) => (
              <button class="article-card" type="button" data-article-slug={article.slug}>
                <span class="article-category">{article.category}</span>
                <h2>{article.title}</h2>
                <p>{article.excerpt}</p>
                <span class="article-open">Read article</span>
                <span class="article-tags" aria-label="Article tags">
                  {article.tags.slice(0, 3).map((tag) => <span>{tag}</span>)}
                </span>
              </button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <p id="blog-empty" class="blog-empty" hidden>No articles match that search.</p>

          <div id="article-reader" class="article-reader" hidden>
            <button id="back-to-articles" class="back-to-articles" type="button">All articles</button>
            {blogArticles.map((article) => (
              <article class="article-full" data-article-full={article.slug} hidden>
                <p class="eyebrow">{article.category}</p>
                <h1>{article.title}</h1>
                <div class="article-full-tags" aria-label="Article tags">
                  {article.tags.map((tag) => <span>{tag}</span>)}
                </div>
                <div class="article-body">
                  {article.body.map((block) =>
                    block.kind === "heading" ? (
                      <h2>{block.text}</h2>
                    ) : (
                      <p set:html={block.html}></p>
                    )
                  )}
                </div>
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script is:inline type="application/json" id="plant-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(plants)}></script>
    <script is:inline type="application/json" id="partner-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(partners)}></script>
    <script is:inline type="application/json" id="plant-art-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(plantArtEntries)}></script>
    <script is:inline type="application/json" id="blog-search-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(blogSearchData)}></script>
    <script is:inline>
      const plants = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("plant-data").textContent);
      const partners = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("partner-data").textContent);
      const plantArtEntries = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("plant-art-data").textContent);
      const blogSearchData = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("blog-search-data").textContent);
      const plantArtById = Object.fromEntries(plantArtEntries.map((entry) => [entry.id, entry]));
      const form = document.getElementById("matcher-form");
      const statusEl = document.getElementById("status");
      const titleEl = document.getElementById("results-title");
      const zoneNoteEl = document.getElementById("zone-note");
      const resultsEl = document.getElementById("results");
      const seeMoreEl = document.getElementById("see-more");
      const saveListEl = document.getElementById("save-list");
      const zipEl = document.getElementById("zip");
      const zonePreviewEl = document.getElementById("zone-preview");
      const tabButtons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll("[data-view]"));
      const viewPanels = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll("[data-view-panel]"));
      const articleSearchEl = document.getElementById("article-search");
      const articleListEl = document.getElementById("article-list");
      const blogEmptyEl = document.getElementById("blog-empty");
      const articleReaderEl = document.getElementById("article-reader");
      const backToArticlesEl = document.getElementById("back-to-articles");
      const articleCards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll("[data-article-slug]"));
      const articleFullViews = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll("[data-article-full]"));
      let currentRanked = [];
      let currentInputs = null;
      let visibleCount = 12;
      const zoneCache = new Map();
      let zoneLookupTimer = null;

      const waterRank = { low: 1, medium: 2, high: 3 };
      const goalLabels = {
        fruit: "fruit",
        "vegetables-herbs": "vegetables & herbs",
        "pollinators-wildlife": "pollinators & wildlife",
        "curb-appeal": "curb appeal & color",
        "privacy-screening": "privacy & screening",
        "low-maintenance-natives": "low-maintenance natives"
      };
      const formLabels = {
        tree: ["tree", "trees"],
        shrub: ["shrub", "shrubs"],
        vine: ["vine", "vines"],
        vegetable: ["vegetable", "vegetables"],
        flowerHerb: ["flower/herb", "flowers/herbs"],
        cactus: ["cactus", "cacti"],
        fruiting: ["fruiting plant", "fruiting plants"]
      };
      const formOrder = ["tree", "shrub", "vine", "vegetable", "flowerHerb", "cactus", "fruiting"];

      function setActiveView(view) {
        tabButtons.forEach((button) => {
          const isActive = button.dataset.view === view;
          button.classList.toggle("is-active", isActive);
          button.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(isActive));
        });
        viewPanels.forEach((panel) => {
          const isActive = panel.dataset.viewPanel === view;
          panel.classList.toggle("is-active", isActive);
          panel.hidden = !isActive;
        });
      }

      function showArticleList() {
        articleReaderEl.hidden = true;
        articleFullViews.forEach((article) => {
          article.hidden = true;
        });
        articleListEl.hidden = false;
        filterArticles();
      }

      function showArticle(slug) {
        setActiveView("blog");
        articleListEl.hidden = true;
        blogEmptyEl.hidden = true;
        articleReaderEl.hidden = false;
        articleFullViews.forEach((article) => {
          article.hidden = article.dataset.articleFull !== slug;
        });
      }

      function filterArticles() {
        const query = articleSearchEl.value.trim().toLowerCase();
        let visibleArticles = 0;
        articleCards.forEach((card) => {
          const article = blogSearchData.find((entry) => entry.slug === card.dataset.articleSlug);
          const isMatch = !query || article?.searchableText.includes(query);
          card.hidden = !isMatch;
          if (isMatch) visibleArticles += 1;
        });
        blogEmptyEl.hidden = visibleArticles > 0;
      }

      tabButtons.forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          setActiveView(button.dataset.view);
        });
      });

      articleCards.forEach((card) => {
        card.addEventListener("click", () => {
          showArticle(card.dataset.articleSlug);
        });
      });

      articleSearchEl.addEventListener("input", showArticleList);
      backToArticlesEl.addEventListener("click", showArticleList);

      function zoneToNumber(zone) {
        const match = String(zone).trim().toLowerCase().match(/^(\d{1,2})([ab])$/);
        if (!match) return Number.NaN;
        return Number(match[1]) + (match[2] === "b" ? 0.5 : 0);
      }

      async function lookupZone(zip) {
        if (zoneCache.has(zip)) return zoneCache.get(zip);
        const response = await fetch(`https://phzmapi.org/${zip}.json`);
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Zone lookup failed");
        const data = await response.json();
        if (!data.zone) throw new Error("Zone missing from lookup");
        zoneCache.set(zip, data);
        return data;
      }

      function buildAffiliateUrl(plant) {
        const partner = partners[plant.partner] ?? partners.amazon;
        const searchUrl = partner.searchUrl.replace("{query}", encodeURIComponent(plant.query ?? plant.name));
        const glue = searchUrl.includes("?") ? "&" : "?";
        return `${searchUrl}${glue}${partner.affiliateParam}`;
      }

      function clamp(value, min, max) {
        return Math.min(max, Math.max(min, value));
      }

      function formatList(values) {
        return values.map((value) => value.replace("-", " ")).join(", ");
      }

      function formatGoal(value) {
        return goalLabels[value] ?? value.replaceAll("-", " ");
      }

      function formatGoalList(values) {
        return values.map(formatGoal).join(", ");
      }

      function sentenceCase(text) {
        return text ? text.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + text.slice(1) : "";
      }

      function plantKind(plant) {
        const type = plant.type.toLowerCase();
        if (type.includes("flower") || type.includes("herb") || type.includes("grass")) return "bloom";
        if (type.includes("vegetable")) return "vegetable";
        if (type.includes("vine")) return "vine";
        if (type.includes("shrub") || type.includes("cane")) return "shrub";
        return "fruit";
      }

      function plantFormKey(plant) {
        const type = plant.type.toLowerCase();
        if (type.includes("tree") || type === "citrus") return "tree";
        if (type.includes("shrub") || type.includes("cane")) return "shrub";
        if (type.includes("vine")) return "vine";
        if (type.includes("vegetable")) return "vegetable";
        if (type.includes("flower") || type.includes("herb") || type.includes("grass")) return "flowerHerb";
        if (type.includes("cactus")) return "cactus";
        return "fruiting";
      }

      function summarizeForms(entries) {
        const counts = entries.reduce((summary, entry) => {
          const key = plantFormKey(entry.plant);
          summary[key] = (summary[key] ?? 0) + 1;
          return summary;
        }, {});
        return formOrder
          .filter((key) => counts[key])
          .map((key) => {
            const count = counts[key];
            const labels = formLabels[key];
            return `${count} ${count === 1 ? labels[0] : labels[1]}`;
          })
          .join(", ");
      }

      function plantIdentity(plant) {
        return `${plant.id} ${plant.name} ${plant.query ?? ""}`.toLowerCase();
      }

      function matchesArtEntry(identity, entry) {
        const matches = entry.match ?? [];
        const excludes = entry.exclude ?? [];
        return matches.some((term) => identity.includes(term.toLowerCase()))
          && !excludes.some((term) => identity.includes(term.toLowerCase()));
      }

      function genericArt(plant) {
        const type = plant.type.toLowerCase();
        if (type.includes("flower") || type.includes("herb") || type.includes("grass") || type.includes("ornamental")) return "generic-flower-herb";
        if (type.includes("vegetable")) return "generic-vegetable";
        if (type.includes("vine")) return "generic-vine";
        if (type.includes("tree")) return "generic-tree";
        return "generic-fruit";
      }

      function plantArtEntry(plant) {
        const identity = plantIdentity(plant);
        return plantArtEntries.find((entry) => matchesArtEntry(identity, entry))
          ?? plantArtById[genericArt(plant)]
          ?? null;
      }

      function plantPhotoStyle(entry) {
        if (!entry?.image) return "";
        const styles = [
          `--plant-photo: url('/plant-art/${entry.image}')`,
          entry.position ? `--photo-position: ${entry.position}` : "",
          entry.plateBg ? `--plate-bg: ${entry.plateBg}` : ""
        ].filter(Boolean);
        return ` style="${styles.join("; ")}"`;
      }

      function scoreBreakdown(plant, inputs) {
        const userZone = zoneToNumber(inputs.zone);
        const minZone = zoneToNumber(plant.zones[0]);
        const maxZone = zoneToNumber(plant.zones[1]);
        const details = [];
        let zoneScore = -120;
        let zoneFit = 0;
        let zoneLabel = "outside range";

        if (userZone >= minZone && userZone <= maxZone) {
          zoneScore = 80;
          zoneFit = 100;
          zoneLabel = "in range";
        } else {
          const distance = userZone < minZone ? minZone - userZone : userZone - maxZone;
          zoneScore = distance <= 0.5 ? 25 : -120;
          zoneFit = distance <= 0.5 ? 42 : 0;
          zoneLabel = distance <= 0.5 ? "borderline" : "poor fit";
        }
        details.push({ label: "Hardiness", value: zoneFit, score: zoneScore, note: `${plant.zones[0]}-${plant.zones[1]} (${zoneLabel})` });

        const goalFit = plant.goals.includes(inputs.goal);
        details.push({
          label: "Goal",
          value: goalFit ? 100 : 0,
          score: goalFit ? 34 : 0,
          note: goalFit ? `matches ${formatGoal(inputs.goal)}` : `better for ${formatGoalList(plant.goals)}`
        });

        let sunScore = -18;
        let sunFit = 0;
        let sunNote = `wants ${formatList(plant.sun)}`;
        if (plant.sun.includes(inputs.sun)) {
          sunScore = 22;
          sunFit = 100;
          sunNote = `takes ${inputs.sun}`;
        } else if (inputs.sun === "partial" && plant.sun.includes("full")) {
          sunScore = 4;
          sunFit = 45;
          sunNote = "borderline in partial sun";
        }
        details.push({ label: "Sun", value: sunFit, score: sunScore, note: sunNote });

        let soilScore = -14;
        let soilFit = 0;
        let soilNote = `prefers ${formatList(plant.soils)}`;
        if (plant.soils.includes(inputs.soil)) {
          soilScore = 16;
          soilFit = 100;
          soilNote = `handles ${inputs.soil}`;
        } else if (inputs.soil === "loam") {
          soilScore = 4;
          soilFit = 55;
          soilNote = "loam is a workable default";
        }
        details.push({ label: "Soil", value: soilFit, score: soilScore, note: soilNote });

        const selectedWater = waterRank[inputs.water];
        const plantWater = waterRank[plant.water];
        let waterScore = -(plantWater - selectedWater) * 18;
        let waterFit = 30;
        let waterNote = `${plant.water} water need`;
        if (plantWater === selectedWater) {
          waterScore = 16;
          waterFit = 100;
          waterNote = `matches ${inputs.water} water`;
        } else if (plantWater < selectedWater) {
          waterScore = 9;
          waterFit = 78;
          waterNote = "will not mind extra water";
        }
        details.push({ label: "Water", value: clamp(waterFit, 0, 100), score: waterScore, note: waterNote });

        let bonus = 0;
        if (plant.type.includes("annual") && inputs.goal === "vegetables-herbs") bonus += 8;
        if (plant.type.includes("fruit") && inputs.goal === "fruit") bonus += 6;
        if (plant.type.includes("perennial") && inputs.goal === "pollinators-wildlife") bonus += 5;
        if ((plant.type.includes("shrub") || plant.type.includes("vine") || plant.type.includes("grass")) && inputs.goal === "privacy-screening") bonus += 6;
        if (plant.water === "low" && inputs.goal === "low-maintenance-natives") bonus += 5;
        if (bonus > 0) details.push({ label: "Use case", value: 100, score: bonus, note: "extra practical fit" });

        const score = details.reduce((sum, detail) => sum + detail.score, 0);
        return { score, details };
      }

      function scorePlant(plant, inputs) {
        return scoreBreakdown(plant, inputs).score;
      }

      function rankingScore(plant, inputs) {
        const base = scorePlant(plant, inputs);
        const userZone = zoneToNumber(inputs.zone);
        const minZone = zoneToNumber(plant.zones[0]);
        const maxZone = zoneToNumber(plant.zones[1]);
        const edgeMargin = userZone >= minZone && userZone <= maxZone ? Math.min(userZone - minZone, maxZone - userZone) : -4;
        const zoneCenter = (minZone + maxZone) / 2;
        const centerPenalty = Math.abs(userZone - zoneCenter) / 20;
        const conditionFit =
          (plant.sun.includes(inputs.sun) ? 0.28 : 0) +
          (plant.soils.includes(inputs.soil) ? 0.2 : 0) +
          (plant.water === inputs.water ? 0.2 : plant.water === "low" && inputs.water !== "low" ? 0.08 : 0);
        const goalSpecificity = plant.goals[0] === inputs.goal ? 0.18 : plant.goals.includes(inputs.goal) ? 0.1 : 0;
        return base + clamp(edgeMargin, -4, 4) * 0.7 - centerPenalty + conditionFit + goalSpecificity;
      }

      function overallFit(score) {
        const percent = clamp(Math.round((score / 180) * 100), 0, 100);
        let label = "Weak";
        let tone = "weak";
        if (percent >= 92) {
          label = "Excellent";
          tone = "excellent";
        } else if (percent >= 82) {
          label = "Strong";
          tone = "strong";
        } else if (percent >= 68) {
          label = "Good";
          tone = "good";
        } else if (percent >= 52) {
          label = "Workable";
          tone = "workable";
        }
        return { percent, label, tone };
      }

      function joinHumanList(values) {
        if (values.length <= 1) return values[0] ?? "";
        if (values.length === 2) return `${values[0]} and ${values[1]}`;
        return `${values.slice(0, -1).join(", ")}, and ${values.at(-1)}`;
      }

      function conditionWins(plant, inputs) {
        const wins = [];
        const userZone = zoneToNumber(inputs.zone);
        if (userZone >= zoneToNumber(plant.zones[0]) && userZone <= zoneToNumber(plant.zones[1])) {
          wins.push(`hardy in zone ${inputs.zone}`);
        }
        if (plant.sun.includes(inputs.sun)) {
          wins.push(inputs.sun === "full" ? "happy in full sun" : `comfortable in ${inputs.sun} sun`);
        }
        if (plant.soils.includes(inputs.soil)) wins.push(`not fussy about ${inputs.soil} soil`);
        if (plant.water === inputs.water) wins.push(`${inputs.water} water is enough`);
        return wins;
      }

      function articleFor(text) {
        return /^[aeiou]/i.test(text) ? "an" : "a";
      }

      function traitPhrase(trait) {
        const tangibleWords = ["fruit", "berries", "berry", "nut", "nuts", "flowers", "foliage", "bloom", "color", "flavor", "texture", "arils", "stems", "spears", "pods", "leaves", "roots", "tubers", "calyces"];
        return tangibleWords.some((word) => trait.includes(word))
          ? `its ${trait}`
          : `being ${articleFor(trait)} ${trait}`;
      }

      function goalLead(plant, inputs) {
        const trait = plant.traits[0];
        const wins = conditionWins(plant, inputs);
        const fit = wins.length ? `; it is ${joinHumanList(wins.slice(0, 2))}` : "";
        if (inputs.goal === "privacy-screening") {
          return `${plant.name} has the bones for screening: ${trait}${fit}.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "pollinators-wildlife") {
          return `${plant.name} earns its place for habitat first: ${trait}${fit}.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "curb-appeal") {
          return `${plant.name} is here because it looks intentional, not just useful: ${trait}${fit}.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "vegetables-herbs") {
          return `${plant.name} is a kitchen-garden pick with a real reason to grow it: ${trait}${fit}.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "low-maintenance-natives") {
          return `${plant.name} fits the low-fuss lane: ${trait}${fit}.`;
        }
        return `${plant.name} earns its slot for ${traitPhrase(trait)}${fit}.`;
      }

      function payoffPhrase(plant) {
        const replacements = [
          [/^ripens in /, "fruit in "],
          [/^ripens from /, "fruit from "],
          [/^often produces /, ""],
          [/^drops ripe fruit in /, "ripe fruit in "],
          [/^bears over /, "fruit over "],
          [/^berries ripen in /, "berries in "],
          [/^berries ripen /, "berries "],
          [/^fruit ripens in /, "fruit in "],
          [/^nuts mature in /, "nuts in "],
          [/^nuts drop in /, "nuts in "],
          [/^spears harvest in /, "spears in "],
          [/^stalks harvest in /, "stalks in "],
          [/^buds form in /, "buds in "],
          [/^edible pads and fruit in /, "pads and fruit in "],
          [/^green onions and bulbils /, "green onions and bulbils "]
        ];
        return replacements.reduce((text, [pattern, replacement]) => text.replace(pattern, replacement), plant.harvest);
      }

      function payoffSentence(plant, inputs) {
        const trait = plant.traits[1] ?? plant.traits[0];
        const payoff = payoffPhrase(plant);
        if (inputs.goal === "pollinators-wildlife") {
          return `The payoff is ${payoff}, plus the movement of bees, birds, or butterflies around it.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "curb-appeal") {
          return `The payoff is ${payoff}, with ${trait} carrying the look.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "vegetables-herbs") {
          return `The payoff is ${payoff}, the kind of harvest that makes the kitchen notice.`;
        }
        if (inputs.goal === "privacy-screening") {
          return `The payoff is ${payoff}, while the plant earns its keep as living structure.`;
        }
        return `The payoff is ${payoff}, with ${trait}.`;
      }

      function explainPlant(plant, inputs) {
        if (plant.id === "mango-pawpaw") {
          return "One of the few large fruits that genuinely handles part shade - perfect for clay-heavy yards where peaches and plums struggle. Slow to fruit (4-6 years), worth the wait. The fruit ripens in early fall with a custardy texture and a flavor between mango and banana; nothing else in a Southern orchard tastes like it.";
        }
        return `${goalLead(plant, inputs)} ${plant.notes} ${payoffSentence(plant, inputs)}`;
      }

      function whyThisWon(plant, inputs) {
        const wins = conditionWins(plant, inputs).slice(0, 2);
        const trait = plant.traits[0];
        return wins.length
          ? `Why it rose: ${sentenceCase(joinHumanList(wins))}, and ${trait}.`
          : `Why it rose: ${sentenceCase(trait)} gives it the strongest read in this search.`;
      }

      function renderFitRows(details) {
        return details
          .map((detail) => {
            const fitClass = detail.value >= 80 ? "good" : detail.value >= 40 ? "okay" : "weak";
            const fitText = detail.value >= 80 ? "strong fit" : detail.value >= 40 ? "workable" : "weak fit";
            return `
              <div class="fit-row ${fitClass}">
                <div class="fit-copy">
                  <span>${detail.label}</span>
                  <strong>${detail.note}</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="fit-meter" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="fit-line"></span>
                  <span class="fit-dot" style="left: ${detail.value}%"></span>
                </div>
                <em>${fitText}</em>
              </div>
            `;
          })
          .join("");
      }

      function renderZoneRange(plant, inputs) {
        const min = 2;
        const max = 11.5;
        const zoneStart = clamp(((zoneToNumber(plant.zones[0]) - min) / (max - min)) * 100, 0, 100);
        const zoneEnd = clamp(((zoneToNumber(plant.zones[1]) - min) / (max - min)) * 100, 0, 100);
        const userPoint = clamp(((zoneToNumber(inputs.zone) - min) / (max - min)) * 100, 0, 100);
        return `
          <div class="zone-range">
            <div class="range-track" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="range-fit" style="left: ${zoneStart}%; width: ${Math.max(2, zoneEnd - zoneStart)}%"></span>
              <span class="range-pin" style="left: ${userPoint}%"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="range-labels">
              <span>Zone ${plant.zones[0]}</span>
              <strong>Your ${inputs.zone}</strong>
              <span>Zone ${plant.zones[1]}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        `;
      }

      function createResultItem(entry, index, inputs) {
        const { plant, score } = entry;
        const item = document.createElement("li");
        const kind = plantKind(plant);
        const artEntry = plantArtEntry(plant);
        const art = artEntry?.id ?? genericArt(plant);
        const hasImage = Boolean(artEntry?.image);
        const photoStyle = plantPhotoStyle(artEntry);
        const detailArt = hasImage
          ? `<figure class="detail-art ${art}" role="img" aria-label="${plant.name} botanical plate"${photoStyle}>
              <span>${plant.name}</span>
            </figure>`
          : "";
        item.className = `result-card ${index === 0 ? "top-card" : ""} ${kind}-card ${art}-art`;

        const partner = partners[plant.partner] ?? partners.amazon;
        const breakdown = scoreBreakdown(plant, inputs);
        const fit = overallFit(score);
        item.innerHTML = `
          <figure class="plant-visual ${kind} ${art} ${hasImage ? "photo-plate" : ""}" aria-hidden="true"${photoStyle}>
            <span class="rank">${index + 1}</span>
            ${hasImage ? "" : `<span class="plant-visual-icon"></span>`}
          </figure>
          <div class="result-copy">
            <div class="result-title">
              <h3>${plant.name}</h3>
              <span>${plant.type}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="overall-fit ${fit.tone}" style="--fit: ${fit.percent}%" aria-label="Overall fit ${fit.percent} percent, ${fit.label}">
              <div class="fit-ring" aria-hidden="true"><span>${fit.percent}</span></div>
              <div>
                <span>Overall fit</span>
                <strong>${fit.label}</strong>
              </div>
            </div>
            ${index === 0 ? `<p class="winner-note">${whyThisWon(plant, inputs)}</p>` : ""}
            <p>${explainPlant(plant, inputs)}</p>
            <div class="trait-row">
              ${plant.traits.slice(0, 2).map((trait) => `<span>${trait}</span>`).join("")}
            </div>
          </div>
          <details class="plant-details ${hasImage ? "has-art" : ""}">
            <summary>
              <span>More data</span>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M7.4 8.6 12 13.2l4.6-4.6L18 10l-6 6-6-6 1.4-1.4Z"></path>
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="details-grid">
              ${detailArt}
              <div class="detail-panel">
                <h4>Fit breakdown</h4>
                <div class="fit-chart">
                  ${renderFitRows(breakdown.details)}
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="detail-panel">
                <h4>Plant data</h4>
                ${renderZoneRange(plant, inputs)}
                <dl class="plant-stats">
                  <div><dt>Sun</dt><dd>${formatList(plant.sun)}</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>Soil</dt><dd>${formatList(plant.soils)}</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>Water</dt><dd>${plant.water}</dd></div>
                  <div><dt>Goals</dt><dd>${formatGoalList(plant.goals)}</dd></div>
                </dl>
              </div>
              <p class="grow-note">${plant.notes}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
          <div class="card-actions">
            <a class="buy-link" href="${buildAffiliateUrl(plant)}" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener">
              ${partner.name}
            </a>
          </div>
        `;
        return item;
      }

      function renderVisibleResults() {
        const visible = currentRanked.slice(0, visibleCount);
        resultsEl.replaceChildren(...visible.map((entry, index) => createResultItem(entry, index, currentInputs)));
        const shownText = currentRanked.length > visibleCount
          ? `Showing the strongest ${visibleCount} of ${currentRanked.length}.`
          : `${currentRanked.length} ranked matches found.`;
        statusEl.textContent = `${shownText} Top picks include ${summarizeForms(visible)}.`;
        if (currentRanked.length > visibleCount) {
          seeMoreEl.hidden = false;
          seeMoreEl.textContent = `See more results (${currentRanked.length - visibleCount} left)`;
        } else {
          seeMoreEl.hidden = true;
        }
      }

      function renderResults(zoneData, inputs) {
        const candidates = plants.filter((plant) => plant.goals.includes(inputs.goal));
        const ranked = candidates
          .map((plant) => ({ plant, score: scorePlant(plant, inputs), rankScore: rankingScore(plant, inputs) }))
          .sort((a, b) => b.rankScore - a.rankScore || b.score - a.score || a.plant.name.localeCompare(b.plant.name));

        titleEl.textContent = `Best ${formatGoal(inputs.goal)} matches for zone ${inputs.zone}.`;
        zoneNoteEl.textContent = zoneData.temperature_range
          ? `USDA average annual extreme minimum: ${zoneData.temperature_range} F. Zone lookup returned coordinates near ${zoneData.coordinates.lat}, ${zoneData.coordinates.lon}.`
          : "Zone lookup succeeded. Local microclimates, chill hours, pests, and drainage still matter.";
        if (ranked.length === 0) {
          statusEl.textContent = "No plants matched that goal. Try a broader goal or loosen one growing condition.";
          resultsEl.replaceChildren();
          seeMoreEl.hidden = true;
          return;
        }

        currentRanked = ranked;
        currentInputs = inputs;
        visibleCount = Math.min(12, currentRanked.length);
        saveListEl.hidden = false;
        renderVisibleResults();
      }

      seeMoreEl.addEventListener("click", () => {
        visibleCount = Math.min(visibleCount + 12, currentRanked.length);
        renderVisibleResults();
      });

      resultsEl.addEventListener("toggle", (event) => {
        const openedDetails = event.target;
        if (!(openedDetails instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) || !openedDetails.classList.contains("plant-details") || !openedDetails.open) return;
        resultsEl.querySelectorAll(".plant-details[open]").forEach((details) => {
          if (details !== openedDetails) details.open = false;
        });
      }, true);

      saveListEl.addEventListener("click", () => {
        if (!currentInputs || currentRanked.length === 0) return;
        const lines = [
          `What Should I Grow - picks for ${currentInputs.zip} / zone ${currentInputs.zone}`,
          "",
          ...currentRanked.slice(0, visibleCount).map((entry, index) => {
            const fit = overallFit(entry.score);
            return `${index + 1}. ${entry.plant.name} (${fit.percent}% ${fit.label}) - ${explainPlant(entry.plant, currentInputs)}`;
          })
        ];
        const blob = new Blob([lines.join("\n")], { type: "text/plain" });
        const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
        const link = document.createElement("a");
        link.href = url;
        link.download = `what-should-i-grow-${currentInputs.zip}.txt`;
        link.click();
        URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
      });

      zipEl.addEventListener("input", () => {
        const zip = zipEl.value.trim();
        clearTimeout(zoneLookupTimer);
        zonePreviewEl.hidden = true;
        zonePreviewEl.textContent = "";
        zonePreviewEl.classList.remove("is-error");
        if (!/^\d{5}$/.test(zip)) return;
        zonePreviewEl.hidden = false;
        zonePreviewEl.textContent = "Checking USDA zone...";
        zoneLookupTimer = setTimeout(async () => {
          try {
            const zoneData = await lookupZone(zip);
            zonePreviewEl.textContent = `Zone ${zoneData.zone} detected`;
            zonePreviewEl.classList.remove("is-error");
          } catch (error) {
            zonePreviewEl.textContent = "Zone lookup needs another try";
            zonePreviewEl.classList.add("is-error");
          }
        }, 350);
      });

      form.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        const formData = new FormData(form);
        const zip = String(formData.get("zip") ?? "").trim();
        const soilInput = String(formData.get("soil"));

        if (!/^\d{5}$/.test(zip)) {
          statusEl.textContent = "Enter a five-digit U.S. ZIP code.";
          return;
        }

        statusEl.textContent = "Looking up your USDA hardiness zone...";
        resultsEl.replaceChildren();
        seeMoreEl.hidden = true;
        saveListEl.hidden = true;

        try {
          const zoneData = await lookupZone(zip);
          const inputs = {
            zip,
            zone: zoneData.zone,
            sun: String(formData.get("sun")),
            soil: soilInput === "not-sure" ? "loam" : soilInput,
            water: String(formData.get("water")),
            goal: String(formData.get("goal"))
          };
          statusEl.textContent = soilInput === "not-sure" ? "Soil set to loam because you selected not sure." : "";
          renderResults(zoneData, inputs);
        } catch (error) {
          titleEl.textContent = "The zone lookup did not respond.";
          zoneNoteEl.textContent = "Try again in a moment, or swap the lookup function to another USDA-zone provider.";
          statusEl.textContent = "No recommendations shown because hardiness zone is required for ranking.";
        }
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
